--------------------------------------------------------------------
CRITERION 3 — both sides of every mutation invalidate.  PASS (with findings)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Lines named, in internal/services/storage/storage.go @ 5eeca01:

  Atomic replace — writeFileLocked (line 371):
    BEFORE: line 401, s.invalidateCache(path), first statement of
            encodeForWrite, called at line 375 before any disk contact.
    AFTER:  line 387, s.invalidateCache(path), after `err = s.atomicWrite(
            path, payload, perm)` at line 379, unconditional, before
            `return err` at 388.

  CreateExclusive (line 436):
    BEFORE: line 401 (same encodeForWrite, called at line 443).
    AFTER:  line 452, after `err = createExclusive(path, payload, perm)`
            at line 447, unconditional, before `return err` at 453.

  removeLocked (line 667), reached by Storage.Remove and ExclusiveWriter.Remove:
    BEFORE: line 672.  AFTER: line 674, straddling `err := os.Remove(path)`
            at line 673.

Merge-resolution question (2a5c068, the encodeForWrite split) answered by
grep: `grep -n "invalidateCache" internal/services/storage/*.go` returns
exactly four call sites (387, 401, 452, 672, 674 — 401 shared by two callers)
and encodeForWrite is called from exactly two places, writeFileLocked:375 and
CreateExclusive:443. The refactor did not create a write path that skips the
pre-invalidation: the single shared helper is the only encoder, and it
invalidates before it encodes. There is exactly one publish site
(storage.go:339) and exactly one generation sample (storage.go:292, before the
os.Stat at 295 as the comment claims).

Two findings for the lead, neither of which fails this criterion as written
(the criterion asks for the lines, and the lines are there):

  F1. CreateExclusive's post-invalidation (line 452) is not covered by any
      test. Deleting only that line and running the whole package:
        $ go test -count=1 ./internal/services/storage/
        ok  budget2/internal/services/storage  32.582s   EXIT=0
      The line is correct and required by the criterion; nothing would notice
      if a future edit removed it.

  F2. Write paths OUTSIDE storage.go reach disk with no invalidation at all:
      migration.go:248-252 (encryptFileWithIdentity), 276-280
      (decryptFileWithIdentity), 300 (rollbackEncryptionWithIdentity), and
      migration.go:49/102/192/193 (verify + marker files). These rewrite real
      data files in place during EnableEncryption/DisableEncryption and never
      touch s.cache or s.cacheGen. This is pre-existing (it predates 06176ef),
      is outside the P16 manifest, and is not a stale-serving hazard of the
      P16 shape because age encryption/decryption necessarily changes the
      file's SIZE, so the mtime+size key cannot match afterwards. Reported
      because the brief asked the question directly. auth.go:93-103 writes
      only .encryption-config.json, which loadConfig reads via os.ReadFile,
      never through the cache.

