CRITERION 5 — uncontended reads still cache.  PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------
TestPublishCacheKeepsEntryFromUncontendedRead (cache_test.go:176-215) passes on
master (criterion 1's -count=3 run). It is not a tautology: mutating
publishCache to never install (`if s.cacheGen != gen || true { return }`, i.e.
the cache degraded to a no-op) makes it fail:
  $ go test -race -count=1 -run TestPublishCacheKeepsEntryFromUncontendedRead -v
      cache_test.go:199: an uncontended ReadFile did not populate the cache
  --- FAIL: TestPublishCacheKeepsEntryFromUncontendedRead (0.00s)   EXIT=1
It asserts both halves: the entry is in s.cache after one read, and a second
read is actually served from it (the file is rewritten behind Storage's back
and the read still returns the cached "AAAA").

